Well, one way to do it is to let the guaranteed demon lords to do the
summoning. A working procedure (that takes quite a lot of patience,
though) is:

1. Genocide black dragons (to prevent nasty accidents with
   disintegration rays killing demon lords prematurely). You may want
   to do the same for umber hulks and blue dragons too, for related
   reasons. 

2. Go into Gehennom and get a couple of the guaranteed demon lords to
   the same level, preferably including both lawful (Asmodeus) and
   chaotic (Orcus, unless I remember incorrectly). Basically, you
   chase the lower lord to upstairs and up until you reach the upper
   one. A cockatrice corpse and spellbook of stone to flesh may make
   this procedure simpler if you want to get all demon lords to same
   level. 

3. Find a nice place of a corridor and burn "Elbereth" there with a
   wand of fire or lightning. An ideal spot would be a straight
   corridor several squares from the upstairs (so that when the demons
   teleport there, they can still cast summoning spells). Then, sit in
   place until all demon lords are summoned. This takes quite a lot of
   time. I haven't checked this from the source, but I get the feeling
   that a scared demon lord is not too likely to summon anything, so
   you might try reverse genociding some spotted jellies around you to
   prevent the demon lords from getting scared from "Elbereth". Also,
   be careful of monsters that don't respect the E-word.

4. If you do not surround yourself with jellies, you can try to kill
   summoned cockatrices and use their corpses to gain some nice
   statues after the demons summon an arch lich or several to the
   scene. This is a good way to gather several dozens of potions of
   gain level and full healing. 

I've managed to get six demon lords to be alive at the same time on
one level. Unfortunately, Yeenoghu and Juiblex got killed for some
reason (probably wands of cold or something like that) before Dispater
and Demogorgon arrived so I didn't get all of them at one time.

